Q: Choosing files in R with RStudio, is there a way to adapt one of three options A: <p>Thanks, did not know about that one and does give both the extended dialog and appears &quot;in front&quot;. I have to find out how filtering works in this option however as I created some added entries in Filter and pass those on from a newly created matrix. An example is:</p>
<pre><code>csv     &quot;Colon separated files (*.csv)&quot;    &quot;*.csv&quot;            
xls     &quot;Excel files (*.xlsx,*.xls)&quot;       &quot;*.xlsx;*.xls&quot;
All     &quot;All files (*.*)&quot;                  &quot;*.*&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>And give user the option to select any of those. Does not seem to work the same as tk_choose.files() in this option. There it is filter = fil[c(&quot;csv&quot;, &quot;xls&quot;, &quot;All&quot;), ] where &quot;fil&quot; contains the full matrix.</p>

Q: Verilog: detect pulses larger than tmax A: <p>How about this.  You will still have to do your check to see if Tmax is exceed, but you get a 1 timescale resolution between results.</p>

<pre><code>always @ (*)
    begin
        while(1)
            begin
            current_time = $realtime; 
            if (last_time &gt; 0.0) freq = 1.0e9 / (current_time - last_time); 
            last_time = current_time; 
            # 1;  // This allows for 1 timescale between loops.  If you leave
                  // this out, most simulators become non-responsive in the loop.
            end
    end
</code></pre>

Q: Pulse ring animation around a Google Maps marker iOS A: <p>somehow it is working now. I created a custom view and set that view into <strong>GMSMarker</strong> <em>iconView</em>. After that added animation into view layer.</p>

<pre><code>UIView *view = [[UIView alloc] initWithFrame:CGRectMake(200, 200, 100, 100)];
view.backgroundColor = [UIColor redColor];
view.layer.cornerRadius = 50;

GMSMarker *m = [GMSMarker markerWithPosition:mapView_.myLocation.coordinate];
m.iconView = view;
m.map = mapView_;


CABasicAnimation *scaleAnimation = [CABasicAnimation animationWithKeyPath:@"transform.scale"];
scaleAnimation.duration = 1.5;
scaleAnimation.repeatCount = HUGE_VAL;
scaleAnimation.autoreverses = YES;
scaleAnimation.fromValue = [NSNumber numberWithFloat:0.1];
scaleAnimation.toValue = [NSNumber numberWithFloat:1.2];

[view.layer addAnimation:scaleAnimation forKey:@"scale"];
</code></pre>

